      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here `default_defaultinfo` and the two module exports are allocated on `GlobalsBuilder`\u0027s heap, but `BuiltinProviders` retains neither that heap nor a module dependency on it. If the caller drops the built `Globals` while keeping `BuiltinProviders` or its preloaded module, which these independent public return values allow, `module.get(\"GnInputsInfo\")` and the default instance dereference freed storage.\n\nCould we allocate the values on a heap owned by the builtin module or retain the source `FrozenHeapRef`?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 91,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 108,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "c122a32e872e908ff7e779063d22c55be8e25163",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a9a73dea_8ceaa16b",
        "filename": "src/gn/starlark/crates/providers/src/providers.rs",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 47,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003023
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-07-22T01:31:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When a caller unpacks through `OwnedFrozenValue::value()` and then drops that owner or its module, the returned `Providers` remains usable but these fields contain `\u0027static` references and raw `FrozenValue`s into the freed heap. Later iterating `value` or expanding a substitution can read freed memory.\n\nCan we make the conversion retain the source `FrozenHeapRef`, require an owned wrapper, or parameterize `Providers` by the input lifetime?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 38,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 47,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "c122a32e872e908ff7e779063d22c55be8e25163",
      "serverId": "c360c8e5-7aa8-3905-a7a0-810934766dac"
    },
